it is no secret that i have been a major  tesla fanboy ever since i first drove  their model s way back in 2014. they had  just introduced the ludicrous mode and i  was blown away by the jaw-dropping  acceleration of that car i mean 0-60 in  under 3 seconds and that too in an  all-electric car for a petrol head like  myself it was almost a spiritual  experience i was convinced on that day  that tesla would become the most  groundbreaking car company in america  and perhaps the entire world and looking  at tesla's growth since that time i  wasn't wrong at all until i drove the  new kid on the block earlier this month  if you read the title of this video i  guess you already know which car i am  referring to here it is the lucid motors  lucid air a friend of mine had just got  the delivery of one of the first lucid  air dream edition and he invited me over  to test it out now mind you i had seen a  lot of pictures of the new car heard a  lot about its performance pedigree and  also seen reviews from auto gurus who  had test driven the vehicle before its  launch but nothing would compare to what  i was going to experience in the next  few minutes of actually driving the car  first on the highways and then in anger  around a local karting track it was at  the end of that day that a thought crept  into my head that people at tesla should  be afraid of this new beast of an  electric vehicle so in this video for  simply tech i am going to share with you  my experience with the lucid air and why  i think tesla should stand up and take  notice of this nissan car brand and its  amazing first model before i get into  why i feel the way i feel about this car  let's set the stage a bit and go over  some of the specifics of this new car  and the company responsible for its  development lucid motors is by no means  a new company it was founded way back in  2007 but it was called ativa until 2016  when it was rebranded as lucid motors  the company in its early days was mostly  focused on manufacturing batteries and  powertrains for other electric vehicle  manufacturers then in 2013 and 2015 two  key personnel changes would see this  small california headquartered company  change dramatically into a full-fledged  electric vehicle manufacturer the first  was peter rawlinson who joined the  company in 2013 as his chief technology  officer before he took this position  rollinson served as the vice president  of vehicle engineering responsible for  the development and delivery of the  first tesla model s the second key  personnel change was the addition of  derek jenkins from the mazda mx-5 hall  of fame jenkins was the head of design  for mazda and joined lucid motors as the  senior vice president of design and  brand in 2015. both these guys would  take the company out of obscurity and by  late 2016 they had rebranded and  announced the development of lucid's  first production all-electric car the  lucid air now you must be thinking  that's all well and good but what's so  good about the car that tesla which is a  giant in the all-electric segment  producing over 200 000 vehicles per year  have to fear well let's take a look at  the specifics then the lucid air is a  full-size luxury sedan that has been  designed from the ground up as an  all-electric vehicle and it shows it has  an epa range of up to 520 miles on a  single charge and can do zero to 60  miles per hour in just under two and a  half seconds but those are just numbers  and even cheap chinese electric car  manufacturers can make an electric car  with those specs on paper no what  separates lucid air and why a giant like  tesla should take notice is what's  inside the car the technological  innovations driving the performance of  the car are staggering in some regards  for example the lucid air claims to be  40 percent more efficient than any other  electric car on the road today in fact  it can travel 17 further than a tesla  model s long range for the same battery  pack size this is because lucid has  managed to improve the efficiency of its  battery pack by working on its layout  and cooling systems within it has  allowed them to extract 4.6 miles per  kilowatt hour which is 15 more efficient  than the tesla model s long range which  has a similar battery size and guess  what that is not even the crazy part the  battery in the lucid air is based around  the formula e race car a global  championship where lucid motor has been  the primary battery supplier since 2018.  rapid development through racing has  allowed lucid motors to shrink the size  of the battery pack and make it more  efficient without sacrificing any safety  or range this racing pedigree is  reflected even better when it comes to  the power train of the car officially  called the pure flux inverter and  transmission unit this is at the heart  of lucid air's sublime performance and  driving experience this is a vertically  arranged powertrain that weighs only 163  pounds but it can deliver 670 horsepower  at 4 400 pounds per foot of torque that  is getting in the range of performance  dragsters and we are talking about a  four-door luxury all-electric sedan here  it can do this because of its permanent  magnet synchronous motors which can spin  it up to 20 000 rpm on both the front  and the rear of the vehicle this  prevents a phenomenon called torque  clogging giving the powertrain more  performance the air's dream performance  edition has a dual configuration of  these motors that can deliver a whopping  111 horsepower that is getting in the  leagues of a formula one car although  the f1 car is way more powerful due to  its low weight this version of the car  can cover a quarter of a mile in 9.8  seconds which absolutely blows my mind  to be honest i have driven almost all  models of tesla cars in tracks and  pretty diverse conditions but never have  i felt such confidence throwing a car  around corners or when flooring the  pedal to the floor due to the weight  distribution of the battery pack and the  drivetrain the air is extremely stable  on its feet even when i was barrel  rolling the lucid air around a race  track at high speeds there was never a  moment where i felt like i was going to  lose control i mean from the  driver-focused comfortable cockpit to  the four-corner suspension system the  air's handling characteristics felt  deserving of its name at this point most  of you guys are wondering well tesla has  a lot of smart features and that is  surely a segment where they are way  ahead of the curve but you would be  wrong thinking that as well lucid air  features a dream drive advanced driver  assistance system that integrates 32  sensors from cameras to ultrasonic  sensors to high-res lidar placed  strategically all over the car  performing various smart autonomous  functions although lucid has not  announced anything like tesla's dojo  chip or its advanced neural net program  which is designed to make the car fully  self-driven i won't be surprised if they  are also planning something similar in  nature for the future you don't put this  many sensors around a car if you didn't  want to leave room to grow and develop  on top of all these features the design  of the air is also quite elegant and  apparently the aerodynamics have been  given extra focus this has allowed the  designers of lucid motors to extract 2  percent more performance just by  sculpting the bodywork to reduce excess  drag this just goes to show how much the  company is driven by efficiency no  wonder then that the company has already  made waves in the automotive industry  and i can confidently say that after  having driven my friends air a few more  times after that first test there is  nothing in the car that i don't like i  mean it can even add range at the rate  of 300 miles per 30 minutes of charging  plus its two-way multifunctional booster  charger the wonderbox is also capable of  vehicle to vehicle charging essentially  allowing you to use your car as a giant  backup battery lucid motors went public  in early 2021 at a valuation of 24  billion dollars within a few months its  valuation blew past general motors 65  billion dollars and then ford's 85  billion dollars it is now one of the  most highly valued car manufacturers in  the u.s and with over 25 000 orders in  2022 which is expected to double next  year it is also fast growing if  rawlinson and jenkins keep delivering on  their promises then i can definitely see  it becoming a major rival of tesla not  only in the domestic u.s market but also  globally within the next five years if i  can draw this conclusion then i am sure  that elon and tesla must have imagined  this scenario as well and if so they  should definitely stand up and take this  challenge posed by lucid air seriously  that's all from my end today i hope all  of you watching get a chance to try out  this awesome electric car yourself and  if you already have do you agree that  tesla should fear lucid air drop a  comment i'd love to know what you guys  think
 

